build: vendor @kmv/platform-shared + Railway deploy config

Make the repo self-contained and deployable. The `file:../platform-shared`
path dependency does not survive a separate-repo deploy — Railway clones
only this repo, so the sibling folder is absent and `pnpm install` fails
(platform-shared README, "Mode B").

- Vendor @kmv/platform-shared's built dist/ into vendor/platform-shared/
  with a trimmed consumer package.json; repoint the dependency to
  file:./vendor/platform-shared. Provenance + re-vendor steps in
  vendor/platform-shared/VENDORED.md. Interim measure — the long-term
  plan is publishing to a private registry (README "Mode A").
- .gitignore: anchor the dist/ rule to /dist/ so it ignores Identiti's
  own build output but not the vendored vendor/platform-shared/dist.
- railway.json: Nixpacks builder, pnpm start, /v1/health check.
- .nvmrc (22) + packageManager pin (pnpm@10.33.0) for deterministic
  Railway builds.
- docs/RAILWAY_DEPLOY.md: deploy steps + env-var checklist (development
  vs staging profiles).

147/147 tests pass; typecheck + build clean; pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
verified.
